      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CERTAINLY QUIET (2) can bounce back third up. She was a dominant maiden winner first up at Bendigo beating a smart one before struggling out to 1700m at Flemington over Cup week. Up to 2100m should suit nicely now and she gets a lovely run on speed. PARIAH PEARL (1) was poor at Flemington in a strong race behind Yauson last start but had been racing well prior. She can roll forward and give a sight. NAVY HEART (3) has been good her past two and now gets Zahra on. She should be ready to peak. ALMAGO (5) has won two on the bounce, handling the drop back in trip last time. Turns around quickly up in trip and can win again. PANDIE PANDIE (7) is only having her third start but looks progressive and has claims.",
